{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"1533","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"H. Submatrices"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"3.5 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"You are given matrix $$$s$$$ that contains $$$n$$$ rows and $$$m$$$ columns. Each element of a matrix is one of the $$$5$$$ first Latin letters (in upper case)."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For each $$$k$$$ ($$$1 \\le k \\le 5$$$) calculate the number of submatrices that contain exactly $$$k$$$ different letters. Recall that a submatrix of matrix $$$s$$$ is a matrix that can be obtained from $$$s$$$ after removing several (possibly zero) first rows, several (possibly zero) last rows, several (possibly zero) first columns, and several (possibly zero) last columns. If some submatrix can be obtained from $$$s$$$ in two or more ways, you have to count this submatrix the corresponding number of times."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line contains two integers $$$n$$$ and $$$m$$$ ($$$1 \\le n, m \\le 800$$$)."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Then $$$n$$$ lines follow, each containing the string $$$s_i$$$ ($$$|s_i| = m$$$) — $$$i$$$-th row of the matrix. "}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"childre